  "body": "### How to reproduce\n\n1. Start an empty project in the desktop app.\n2. Import one part, such as a small STL box.\n3. Open **Stock** and select **From model**.\n4. Check that **Source** shows the part name. Click **Apply**.\n\n**Actual result.** The form can submit an empty source name. Stock creation fails. Opening the picker and clicking its only entry still leaves the draft empty.\n\n**Expected result.** Apply creates stock from the part shown in Source. The user can accept the displayed selection without changing it first.\n\n### Evidence\n\nA user reported this on macOS with one imported STL. On desktop build `e6e04f5d0`, the source field starts empty. The picker displays the last eligible model as its default. It writes the name to the draft only when the selection index changes. Apply reads the draft. With one model, the index cannot change.\n\nOn the same build, passing the model name explicitly to MCP `set_stock` with `from_model` succeeded for that STL. After saving and reopening the project, the setup retained the source name and the stock bounds matched the model bounds. A synthetic part is sufficient for the regression test.\n\n**Done means:** A UI test imports one model, selects From model and clicks Apply without changing Source. It checks the resulting stock and its source name. With several models, the name submitted must also match the name shown.\n\nSuggested triage: bug, P3, effort:medium, area:ui, source:agent. The workaround uses MCP. The fix concerns the UI draft for an existing command.\n\n[Stock source picker](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/e6e04f5d0/crates/ui/src/egui_app/stock_page.rs#L101-L124)\n",
